# Moved from bootstrap/examples/layout-self.moss. Verdicts below credited to the
# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# D58 (AUDIT-CHANGES #90): a tag that contains itself unboxed has no finite
# layout (a value is a run of scalars, D59). `LCell`'s payload is a record
# whose field `tail` is `LNil | LCell`: computing LCell's layout computes
# LCell's. tests/wasi/cyclic.moss with no prelude items.
# Verdicts: oracle rejects ("`LCell` contains itself, so it has no finite
# layout (D58)"); native rejects ("this type has no finite runtime layout");
# Audit before #90 accepts, now rejects (FiniteLayouts).
tag LNil;
tag LCell { head: (), tail: LNil | LCell };
fn main() { let c = LCell { head = (), tail = LNil }; }
